# Origin of the live, public Bubble API (served by the Discord bot).
# Used by src/lib/live-api.ts for the leaderboard, catch feeds and server
# directory on /leaderboard, plus the homepage stats strip.
#
# See DEPLOY_LIVE_API.md in this repo for the full two-step setup (hosting
# the bot's API + setting this var at BUILD time on your deploy platform —
# a local .env file alone does nothing for a deployed site).
#
# IMPORTANT: this value is baked into the browser bundle at build time, so it
# must be a URL that VISITORS can reach. "localhost" only works while you are
# developing on the same machine as the bot — on the deployed site it makes the
# visitor's own browser call their own computer, which is why the live
# leaderboard shows "Live data is offline".
#
# Local development (bot running on the same machine):
# VITE_BUBBLE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
#
# Production: expose the bot's API on a public HTTPS host (reverse proxy,
# Cloudflare Tunnel, VPS domain, etc.) and point this at it:
# VITE_BUBBLE_API_URL=https://api.yourbubbledomain.com
#
# The bot API must also send CORS headers allowing your website origin:
#   Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://yourwebsite.com
#   Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, OPTIONS
#   Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type
# and answer OPTIONS preflight requests with 204.
#
# Leave this empty to hide the live widgets behind a clear "not configured"
# notice instead of failing requests.
VITE_BUBBLE_API_URL=
